{"content":[{"c":["ACHAN, ACHAR*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Member of Judah’s tribe who kept some of the spoils from the Israelite victory at Jericho in violation of Joshua’s order and God’s command (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.6.1-7.1","r":"Josh.6.1-7.1","rawR":"Josh.6.1-7.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.6.1-7.1","value":"Josh.6.1-7.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 6:1–7:1"},"). A subsequent Israelite defeat at Ai, a weaker city than Jericho, revealed God’s anger to Joshua. With God’s help, Joshua determined which of the Israelites had been guilty of disobedience. Achan confessed that he had buried a robe and some gold and silver from Jericho in his tent (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.7.20-22","r":"Josh.7.20-22","rawR":"Josh.7.20-22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.7.20-22","value":"Josh.7.20-22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 7:20-22"},"). The recovered loot was taken to the valley of Achor (meaning “trouble,” “calamity”), where Achan and his family were stoned. In the Hebrew text, ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.2.7","r":"1Chr.2.7","rawR":"1Chr.2.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.2.7","value":"1Chr.2.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chronicles 2:7"}," gives Achan’s name as Achar (“disaster”) because he “brought disaster on Israel by taking plunder that had been set apart for the ",{"c":["Lord"],"sourceClass":"divine-name","t":"span"},"” (",{"c":["nlt"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"AchanAchar","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jos 6:1–7:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.6.1-7.1","rawQueryValue":"Josh.6.1-7.1","sourceRefExact":"Josh.6.1-7.1"},{"anchorText":"Jos 7:20-22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.7.20-22","rawQueryValue":"Josh.7.20-22","sourceRefExact":"Josh.7.20-22"},{"anchorText":"1 Chronicles 2:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.2.7","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.2.7","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.2.7"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"7a897dd28f07dc8b3a798a97328aeaa7a8cf7d3e5c769fc5ae4f149bd256b8c9","sourceItemName":"AchanAchar","sourceItemOrder":76,"sourceMember":"Articles/A.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"AchanAchar","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Achan, Achar*","title":"Achan, Achar*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}